5
00:00:21,446 --> 00:00:25,829
main was protected by a classic branch
protection rule, created years ago.

6
00:00:25,869 --> 00:00:29,356
The person who force-pushed was
a repository administrator.

7
00:00:29,396 --> 00:00:33,301
And under a classic rule, administrators
are not bound by default.

8
00:00:33,641 --> 00:00:37,937
The rule was active. It targeted the
right branch. It contained the right

9
00:00:37,977 --> 00:00:42,867
restriction. It did not apply to the person
who pushed, and nobody on the team knew

10
00:00:42,907 --> 00:00:46,550
that, because only administrators
can even see a classic rule.

11
00:00:46,890 --> 00:00:51,508
Your CTO's follow-up is the right one:
what else do we have that only looks

12
00:00:51,548 --> 00:00:55,855
protected? This video goes through
the remaining pieces: tags, pushes,

13
00:00:55,895 --> 00:01:00,948
organization-wide rules, the classic
mechanism, and what your plan lets you use at

14
00:01:00,988 --> 00:01:04,426
all. Keep the CTO's question.
We answer it door by door.

15
00:01:06,266 --> 00:01:10,777
